        "ratings": [
            {
                "comment": "He is very straight-forward in lecture. Exams reflect that. Best of the 3! book is not necessary!",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 3
            },
            {
                "comment": "Clear and engaging lecturer, I enjoyed going to his lectures. He wants everyone to love genetics like he does. If you do the readings before class his lectures are very easy to follow.",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "Good, clear lectures. Tested on a lot of little concepts, so beware of that.",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "I really enjoyed learning from Dr. Wolman! You could tell that he really has a passion for genetics and that he wants to see his students succeed.",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "He explains difficult concepts so well, and helps solidify content with a little review before lecture (still study up). He goes a little fast through content, but comfortable enough where you can keep up in class. Very organized, well spoken, and my favorite of the 151 professors.",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "One of the best professors (and classes) I have had at UW. The exams are short answer which requires you to have a good understanding of the material so I feel like I learned a lot from. Take good notes in class - exams are open note!  Always willing to meet outside of class to answer questions and chat about his research. Best professor ever!",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "The best bio 151 professor there is no counter argument",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Overall, Dr. Wolman was a good prof. Exams are primarily based off of lecture, so be sure to take good notes and watch online videos if you miss a class. Textbook can be helpful to clarify anything that's confusing. He wants everyone to ace the exam, so if you put in the effort to learn, getting an A on the exam is not unreasonable.",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "Dr. Wolman was my least favorite of our three lecturers; he wasn't bad--just not my style. He's a cool guy, but I didn't get much from his forgetful power point  lectures that he flew through, so I relied mostly on the book for his section.",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "Professor Wolman was the best lecturer of the three section course. It was the easiest and the most clear to students. He highlighted important points and always responded to emailed questions. As someone with not much background in biology, I felt like he really helped me understand the material unlike the other two professors. Textbook helpful.",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "My favorite professor of three in the class. His slides explain material well, and as long as you pay attention in lecture you will be fine. His exam was fair and reading wasn't necessary as long as you understood the material.",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Not the best instructor and really ruses through material. He just talks behind vague figures and slides. Also, he constantly drinks his coffee and talks in a droll voice that gives off the impression he doesn't want to be here. ",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 3
            },
            {
                "comment": "He was an okay professor. It was his first year teaching bio 151, but it wasn't too bad. READ THE BOOK more than studying your lectures. ",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 3
            }
